# 12. Important backend/API behavior

Do not change the existing backend unnecessarily.

First inspect how the current Export functionality works.

Determine:

* What API is called
* Whether the API request remains open until the Excel is generated
* Whether the response directly contains the Excel file
* How the frontend currently triggers the browser download
* Whether multiple export requests are possible simultaneously

Then integrate the UI around the existing behavior.

If the current API only returns the Excel when the generation is complete, use the API request lifecycle:

```text
Request started → In progress

Response received → Completed + trigger browser download
```

Do not invent backend progress tracking.

If the current architecture already has an export job/status mechanism, use that instead.

